  "interfaces": {
    "input": "Natural A(2m), m even>=8, actual string C-marking of rankm; transitive binary maximal omission H, all H_j intransitive; l swaps rows and has exactly two noncommuting neighbours r,s.",
    "additional_conditional_hypothesis": "The full contracted r,s graph J is connected on precisely four l-pairs Y and has only isolated vertices outside Y. The general reduction to this case is not a theorem of this packet and is not silently acquired.",
    "induction": "Alternating bound floor((q-1)/2) explicitly assumed at every12<=q<2m, with the acquired exact lower-degree maxima, exactly as needed by the completed pair-block theorem.",
    "graph": "The distinctly reviewed common support and bridge proof applies. New additional-edge confinement uses actual eligible edges and genuine pair permutations of C marks only; r,s are never asserted to act on contracted vertices.",
    "actual_forms": "The two mixed/swapping forms are derived from the support lemma, actual commutation and the four-pair condition, without a census premise.",
    "uniform_words": "Two displayed actual permutation identities recover r in <l,s,g> in the mixed case; their full point images are given. In the both-swapping case an explicit eight-point walk makes H_l transitive through the selected bridges.",
    "new_pair_maximality": "The central permutation z need not lie in H. Actual intransitive omission sections give faithful genuine C-markings on the new pairs; complete L047 and the extremal independent-generator theorem prove maximality before the pair-block theorem is used."
  },
